  "body": "When an image is loaded. The corresponding thumbnail on the image is centered and shown as selected in the filmstrip, but there's no other visual cue to indicate which thumbnail corresponds to the image. I can click on another thumbnail (single click, not loading that image) and scroll the filmstrip and I then loose reference of the currently shown image:\n\n<img width=\"350\" height=\"277\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3099e6ce-d9ad-477c-81d3-6be1df00de9c\" />\n\nLeft thumbnail corresponds to loaded image, right thumbnail is another image after I click on this thumbnail.\nMaybe a persistent border such as the one shown in orange can be used with a different color.",
